{
  "dom_id": "step-q121005",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Solve the equation $\\sqrt{5}-5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=\\sqrt{5}$ for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation, isolating $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}-5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x & =\\sqrt{5} \\\\ -5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the solutions to $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=0$ correspond to the roots of $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.$ \n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(0)={90}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${90}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={90}^{\u2218}.$\n\nThis solution is a quadrantal angle. To find the remaining solutions, we use our knowledge of the cosine function. We know that the cosine function has its roots at\n\n$$\nx={90}^{\u2218}+{180}^{\u2218}\\cdot n.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to find the other solution ${x}_{2}$ in the given range, we set $n=1,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={90}^{\u2218}+{180}^{\u2218}={270}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x={90}^{\u2218},\\,{270}^{\u2218}.$",
